Negative control for filter-scorecard.test.ts.

Stops the button group's tester scoring `options.format`, so it claims EVERY
enumerated boolean leaf instead of the ones asking for it. The scorecard's
"exactly one renderer, and these decline" assertions go red — the toggle group's
leaf now carries two claimants, and a leaf naming no format at all is claimed
rather than left to the generic control. An assertion that only checked the
button group still claims its own leaf, at rank 3, stays green.

diff --git a/packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/FilterButtonGroupRenderer.vue b/packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/FilterButtonGroupRenderer.vue
index da4dcaec9..886945dd9 100644
--- a/packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/FilterButtonGroupRenderer.vue
+++ b/packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/FilterButtonGroupRenderer.vue
@@ -65,10 +65,6 @@ const positions = computed<ButtonGroupItem[]>(() =>
 <script lang="ts">
 export const tester = {
   rank: 3,
-  controlType: and(
-    isBooleanControl,
-    isEnumControl,
-    optionIs("format", "button-group")
-  )
+  controlType: and(isBooleanControl, isEnumControl)
 };
 </script>
